WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.928
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.050
SPEAKER: It's possible to
use BigQuery to analyze data

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.110
without a credit card by
setting up the BigQuery sandbox

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.380
environment.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.010
This video will show you how
to set up your own BigQuery

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.810
sandbox.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.450
Start by navigating
to the BigQuery Web UI

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:29.980
at console.cloud.go
ogle.com/bigquery.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.740
Log into your Google account,
or create a new account

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.270
if you do not already have one.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.920
If you are logging into Google
Cloud for the first time,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.680
you will need to
choose your country

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.350
and accept the terms of service.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.700
Click Agree and Continue.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.680
In order to use the
BigQuery sandbox,

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.700
you must create a project.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:04.440
Enter a project name,
and click Create.

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.170
Once the project
is created, you'll

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.830
be redirected to
the BigQuery Web UI.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.840
Notice the sandbox
banner indicator

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.750
in the upper left-hand
corner of the console.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.940
Congratulations, you
are now ready to start

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.040
using the BigQuery sandbox.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.200
You can load or query
data in this project

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.810
without an attached
billing account.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.030
Usage will be limited to the
same limits as the free tier,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.740
which can be viewed at
cloud.google.com/free.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.280
Any tables, views, or
partitions and partition tables

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.640
automatically expire
after 60 days.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.530
To overcome these
sandbox limits,

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.240
you can choose to
upgrade your project

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.840
by enabling billing and removing
or updating the expiration

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.730
time for your resources.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:50.990
Happy analyzing.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.040
[MUSIC PLAYING]

